Report databases with mixed utf8mb3 collations.

A database whose tables were created either side of the MariaDB 11.5
change to character_set_collations holds columns in both
utf8mb3_general_ci and utf8mb3_uca1400_ai_ci. Nothing fails until a
migration joins one to the other, so the state stays invisible.

Report it from the MariaDB check, the only pass that runs after the
service migrations which create the mixture. The query inspects columns
rather than table defaults because columns are what a join compares, and
it warns rather than failing since the deployment itself still works.

Prompt: Michael pointed out that the precheck this started as runs
before any schema exists, so it could never see the mixture it looked
for. This moves the same query to the post-deployment check.

